* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * **			                  **      A P P L E   I I g s   I N S T A L L E R   P R O G R A M   V  2 . 1     **                                                                             **                              by "Jay" Schaffer                              **                               and  Ron Lichty                               **			                  ** This program permits adding, replacing, and/or deleting files on a volume   ** based on instructions contained in a 'script' file.	                  **			                  **  Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1987-1992              All Rights Reserved  **			                  ** * * * * * * * * *	* * * * * * * * * *	* * * * * * * * * *	* * * * * * * * * *;______________________________________________________________________________;;          B U I L D - D A Y    I N S T R U C T I O N S;______________________________________________________________________________Release Notes.Installer  update to note Installer/System versions and build date.Version.macros	update Installer version and build date.Installer.r	update Installer rVersion.Search for 'brk'.Do a build or a full build:  Prove it’s working.Project / Mount A.U.G.	Double-click Installer (in Check-Out Window)Project / Check In...	Select All	Keep Modifiable (unless you're going out of town)Build / Installer -> Pasta for TestingVersion.macros	update Installer version and build date.Installer.r	update Installer rVersion.rewrite Release Notes.Installer to Word document	Alfredo: Release Notes: 6.1 Release Notes: 6.1 Release Notes;______________________________________________________________________________;;          E R S - R E L E A S E    I N S T R U C T I O N S;______________________________________________________________________________Update:	cut in any graphics	date and version on front cover	date and Installer version on Revision History	Appendix E (the Standard Update Script)	Appendix G (Testing Recommendations)print a copyreview for page breaksredo Table of Contents for new page numbersprint Table of Contents2 single-sided copies for meoriginal -> Kirk for distribution, double-sided, including one to my archiveselectronic -> Lee, Kirk;______________________________________________________________________________;;          R E V I S I O N   H I S T O R Y   V e r s i o n   2 . 0;______________________________________________________________________________; V2.0 is an almost total rewrite of the Installer program.  The biggest changes; include conversion to GS/OS Class 1 calls, elimination of macros (except for; 'Version.Macros', addition of program segmentation, and the extensive use of; resources.;______________________________________________________________________________; 20 Mar 90 V2.0d1	Initial release for user interface testing of the Custom;	Installation dialog.  Code is still pretty shaky but every-;	thing is there and sort-of working.  (DESIGINATED V2.0X); - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 20 Mar 90	Converted ApplicationDir to a dynamically allocated GStr in;	preparation to eliminating hierarchy depth limitations.; 21 Mar 90	Filetype $04 still recognized as script, however,;	filetype $B0 with auxtype $0017 or $0018 is also recognized.;  3 Apr 90	Completed implementation of:;	  - new data structures for storing full pathnames of script;	    files.;	  - use of prefix #8 to permit l-o-n-g prefixes.;	  - eliminated hierarchical depth limitations.;  4 Apr 90 V2.0d2	Fixed a bug connected with triple clicking on a destination;	folder name.;	Implemented Icons in the PopUp menu.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 12 Apr 90 V2.0d3	Worked with Harry to fix MenuMgr and made alterations in my;	implementation of PopUp menus with icons to match.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 16 Apr 90	Added a general purpose talking-head message box that can;	be used to notify user of what's happening when there are;	delays in continuing (such as: stand-by...searching for scripts.; 17 Apr 90	Fixed a bug that was causing the open button not to be;	activated and deactivated properly in all cases.; 23 Apr 90	Added a null field to the end of the icon file so that the;	Finder wouldn't go off to never-never land looking for the;	next icon.; 25 Apr 90	Added code to create a null list when deactivating the;	application selection window and to create a legitimate;	list during activation.;	Added code to delete all PopUp menu items when the PopUp;	is deactivated.;	Fixed a bug that was preventing the New Folder control from;	properly becoming active.; 26 Apr 90 V2.0d4	Added code to declare the Application Folder Selection;	window as a "ValidRect" after the list is redrawn so that;	Taskmaster will not redraw it a second time.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  7 May 90	Implemented code to add scripts found in the root directory;	of any on-line volume.;  8 May 90	Reinstalled the old original Heapsort--something is wrong;	with the later one that doesn't sort properly.; 14 May 90 V2.0d5	Finished implementing script searching to include adding;	scripts to the list that were double clicked.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 23 May 90	Implemented disk scanning and adding scripts from "just-;	inserted" volumes.; 29 May 90	Moved everything to /Install6.0 disk and changed Icons file.; -- --- --	Much testing and bug fixing!;  2 Jul 90 V2.0d6	Added code to permit any readable block device to appear;	as a potential destination volume, but with INSTALL and;	REMOVE dimmed if the the volume is not write-enabled.; . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .;  7 Jul 90	Added the Standard Update help screen.; 20 Jul 90	Re-sized both dialogs and added key-equivalent info to;	buttons, as appropriate.  Added arrow buttons for switching;	back and forth between the two dialogs.; 23 Jul 90 V2.0d7	Revised initialization so that current disk and current;	volume remain unchanged when switching back and forth;	between the two dialogs.; NOTE:  Version number was accidently NOT updated.  This release appears as;        V2.0d6 dated 23 Jul 90!; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 30 Jul 90	Added code to dim "Begin Standard Update" when disk cannot;	be installed upon.;  1 Aug 90	Eliminated call to alter GS/OS preferences.  (Let GS/OS ask;	for disks as needed.; 13 Aug 90	Added code to catch duplicate disk insertions.; 25 Sep 90	Install.asm now operational with full SuperScript implemen-;	tation!  Begin Standard Update is the only major piece left.; 26 Sep 90	Found an error in DrawFilename (called by UpdateMsgWindowRead;	and UpdateMsgWindowWrite) that was setting the GrafPort back;	to an invalid address.; 26 Sep 90 V2.0d8	BRC #73799 - Left out an AND #$00FF in NewFolderSub when I;	was looking for a trailing SeparatorChar.  Thus, I kept;	appending another separator everytime the user tried again;	to correct a bad name.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 29 Sep 90	BRC #74101 - Removed an extra PHA when calling _Alert on a;	script that requires that the help field be displayed.;  3 Oct 90	BRC #74112 - Eliminated requirement that there must be a;	"9:SCRIPTS" folder.  "No scripts found" is only reported;	now after all possible script locations have been searched.;  3 Oct 90	BRC #74102 - Added code at beginning of Error handler to;	assure it will do absolutely nothing if it receives a;	"Volume Not Found" error (GS/OS is handling that now).; 10 Oct 90	Got the "Begin Standard Update" button running, installing;	from a script resource in the Installer program.  {THE LAST;	FEATURE IS NOW IN PLACE.}; 17 Oct 90 V2.0d9	Got the first part of the supporting code to operate.  I;	can install System:Start and System:Finder appropriately.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 24 Oct 90 V2.0d10 Reimplemented the code to support the StandardUpdateScript;	such that it appends FileSpecFields to the end of the;	script as needed to install Start, Finder, UniDisk3.5,;	SCSIHD.Driver, and SCSI.Manager.  Revised script to reflect;	new volume name of ":Install:" and new locations of some;	files.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 31 Oct 90	Repaired a bug in reading the SYSTEM:START file to determine;	what it contains.;  1 Nov 90	BRC #69391 - Widened the Standard Update dialog box to handle;	the longest possible HFS volume name.;  	BRC #74115 - Replaced an erroneous JSL with the proper JSR.;  2 Nov 90	Added some missing variable initialization that was preventing;	a Standard Update from taking place if the user merely ran;	the Installed and hit "Begin Standard Update" button to install;	on the the boot disk.;  3 Nov 90	The SYS.RESOURCES file on the boot disk CAN NO LONGER be;	closed--it is being used by tools that the Installer relies;	on and will cause a fatal error if it is closed.;	     Therefore,  if we get a "Duplicate File" error, it is;	assumed that we have encountered the SYS.RESOURCES file on;	the boot disk, since we should be able to delete anything;	else before we try to _CREATE a new file.;	     Whenever a "Duplicate File" error is encountered, a;	write is simulated to keep the thermometer dial on track;	but the write never actually occurs!;	Amazing!  GS/OS _Volume call returns a "Not a ProDOS disk";	error on an HFS volume even though the HFS.FST is present!;	On the disk scan, I've special-cased o ignore this error.;	Added ReBootDialog to StandardUpdate quit sequence.  (Not;	sure how I overlooked that before!);  4 Nov 90 V2.0d11	(It appears that V2.0d10 released as a disk image did not;	get saved correctly.  Everyone has had trouble with it.  So;	I am re-releasing today as a new version.); - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  6 Nov 90	Changed StandardUpdate script so that all fonts except;	FastFont and Tools 025, 026, and 029 are "Update"s.;	Fixed a bug in the ScanDevices routine with Dave Lyons';	help.  Pointer needed one more dereference to be safe.;	Removed the WindowColor as a resource from the rWindParam1;	resources.  Dave Lyons descovered a bug in the Window Mgr;	when trying to deal with a color table as a resource.;	ReadBufEnd was being set before the StandardUpdate script;	was being amended!  That goofed up DeleteField's _BlockMove!;  7 Nov 90 V2.0d12	{Released after midnight.} A component of System 6.0d19.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 12 Nov 90	Added code to prevent using "Begin Standard Update" button;	if the destination is anything other than a ProDOS format;	disk.;	Made right and left arrow keys active for going back and;	forth between the two dialogs.; 13 Nov 90	Fixed a bug in Check4Scripts that was not testing for the;	correct script FileType and AuxType.; 14 Nov 90 V2.0d13	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 15 Nov 90	Added code to NewFolderSub to set the system prefix to the;	full pathname describing the just-created folder and added;	code to move the name into application directory name.;	{{•••This may have fixed a whole bunch of bugs!•••}}; 19 Nov 90	Fixed a mess associated with the dialog to notify the user;	we calculate space on 'foreign' volumes.;	Converted the "Done" message to a subroutine so it could be;	added to Standard Update.; 20 Nov 90	Changed wording of completion messages in hopes of;	clarifying what has really happened.;	Added a missing dereference ahead of an <AppDirPtr access.;	This fixed the bugs pertaining to system hang when clicking;	on the ADU script.;	Added a little subroutine to check volume for write-protect;	and foreign format.;	Utilized the old "Installer's volume" bit (15) in the;	InstallRemoveMode word to indicate write-protection.; 21 Nov 90	Fixed MakeFile to create Installer with FileType = $B3 and;	AuxType = $DB07.; 21 Nov 90 V2.0d14	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 27 Nov 90	Widened the PopUp menu to accomodate the longest possible;	HFS volume name without truncating.  (NOTE: Change the;	rectagle definition in resourced AND the width definition;	for _CalcMenuSize in MainSub.asm to change PopUp size.);	Added code to skip script list building if there are no;	scripts in the SCRIPTS folder.; 28 Nov 90	Changed a BNE to a BCC in the UpdatePopUp code which was;	causing a crash if there were no volumes on line and the;	CurDir name was null.; 28 Nov 90 V2.0d15	Signed into Projector to be included on system build 2.0d20.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 30 Nov 90	Added to code to switch to "watch" cursor whenever the;	OpenMsgWindow is called and to switch to the "arrow";	cursor when CloseMsgWindow is called.;	Added delay code to pace device scanning at about 1 sec.;  3 Dec 90	PopUp menu still not wide enough to display icon and longest;	possible folder name.  Boy!  It REALLY looks silly now!;  4 Dec 90	Changed "startup" to "start up" in help screen.;  5 Dec 90	Fixed a bug in the InstallSUB/RemoveSub error exit routines.;	If the script got cancelled, things really got screwed up!;  5 Dec 90 V2.0d16	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  5 Dec 90	Corrected an oversight in the CompareNames subroutine.  The;	destination pathname is NOT fully expanded when the Standard;	Update script is running.  Therefore, it is necessary to get;	a temporary buffer and fully expand it to make the comparison.;;  5 Dec 90 V2.0d17	Part of system 6.0d21 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 10 Dec 90	Fixed a bug in the routine to compare the current directory;	with the boot volume name during system level installations.;;	Removed the SimpleKeyFilter as an input parameter to the;	ReBoot dialog's _Alert call.  It caused a bomb.  Need a;	logic analyzer to trouble shoot it.;	Removed and erroneous error handler call in the ScanDevices;	subroutine that was causing errors to be reported on such;	things as a "Device not connected" when there was a CDROM;	drive on line but nothing mounted; 12 Dec 90	Added code to advance to the next online when the current;	disk is manually ejected.; 12 Dec 90 V2.0d18	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 13 Dec 90	Discovered that if a file was too large to copy in one pass;	and the TooSmallFlag was being set, it was not getting;	cleared again if the next file had an empty data fork, such;	as a CDev.; 13 Dec 90 V2.0d19	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 13 Dec 90	Added code to determine if a "File is already open" error is;	caused by attempt to delete Sys.Resources on boot volume.;	If so, file is closed and deleted and Sys.Resources on the;	:Install disk is opened for read only.; 14 Dec 90	Fixed a bug in the AmendScript routine that was not properly;	adding the START and FINDER FileSpec fields to the script;	when appropriate.;	Revised DeleteFile so that it could return some errors;	rather than ignore all errors.  (Of course, only a few could;	possibly occur by this time, but we only really wanted to;	ignore those generated if there was no file to delete.); 14 Dec 90 V2.0d20	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 17 Dec 90	Fixed a bug in Startup.asm that was removing the trailing;	separator character from the boot volume name string, then;	spreading the faulty string around to everyone, including;	the PopUp, which didn't like it at all!; 18 Dec 90 V2.0d21	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 18 Dec 90	Not in the right bank when the QuitFlag was initially cleared;	as the Installer is first starting up.  Changed to long;	address.;	Fixed a typographical error in operand syntax when loading;	registers to call CheckVolume.;	Oops!  I created a bug with my fix of the ScanDevice routine;	to make it advance to the next on removals.  Now OK.; 18 Dec 90 V2.0d22	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 20 Dec 90	Added code to build a new list for the Application Folder;	selection window following a manual disk ejection.;	Added code to do a NewList2 call after adding more scripts;	to the list following a disk insertion.;	Converted CurrentVol to a string with a trailing colon.  (It;	was inconsistent before and causing problems.)  Identified;	every routine using CurrentVol and modified as needed.;	Implemented a work-around for a problem presented by the;	ResourceMgr when I wanted to shut-down the Sys.Resources;	file.  Seems it was part of another resource search path;	and everything was getting screwed up by the time I finished;	trying to switch to the Install disk's Sys.Resources file.; 20 Dec 90 V2.0d23	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 21 Dec 90	Back-tracked to eliminate Converting CurrentVol to include;	a trailing colon.  It really should have been done, but to;	try and do it now breaks far too many things!  Must find;	another way to fix the comparison in CheckForReboot.;	Removed the trailing colon from the VolStr (boot volume;	name) after distributing it to everyone so it would be of;	the correct format for comparing with the string at;	CurDirPtr later.; 21 Dec 90 V2.0d24	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  2 Jan 91	Revised BuildDirName to handle the situation where the;	volume name and the final folder name are too long to fit,;	as they might be with very long HFS names.;  3 Jan 91	Changed all copyright notices to include 1991.;	Oops!  I should have used long addressing to remove the;	trailing colon in VolStr (see above) because the StartUp;	segment may not be in the same bank with Data.asm.;  3 Jan 91 V2.0d25	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  3 Jan 91	Added a GetCurDirPtr call to CheckForReboot to be sure that;	CurDirPtr is set correctly everytime through.;	String at CurDir should be stored without a trailing colon.;	String at AppDir should be stored with a trailing colon.;	Added code to handle no volumes on line when switching;	between the dialogs.;  3 Jan 91 V2.0d26	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  4 Jan 91	Fixed a bug that came from the days of Customized Install as;	the only dialog where I was initializing the 1st PopUp menu;	item with the contents of <CurDirPtr.  Changed to contents;	of CurrentVol since <CurDirPtr could point to a full path;	when re-entering Customized Installation and we wanted only;	the volume name.;  4 Jan 91 V2.0d27	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;	Added a long address in GetCurDirPtr since it may be called;	from another bank.;  4 Jan 91 V2.0d28	Part of system 6.0d22 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;   First fixes by rdl.;   Optimized GStrNew and GStrResize.;   Fixed bugs in CompareNames and rewrote it for size: 1st bug Greg Branche found,;handle that was being allocated under Standard Update, but was being disposed of ;regardless of Standard Update or not.  Second bug involves failed call to GStrResize;due to string sent to Expand_Path being longer than buffer available to put it in.;Lots of optimizations.;   Fixed bug in GStrNew: string size was being sign-extended rather than zero-extended.; 22 Jan 91 V2.0d29	Part of system 6.0d23 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 23 Jan 91	Install.Asm: Fixed bug: that occasionally caused;	8-minute delays between "Stand by..." message and "Calculating;	space" message: Just after NextDevice, DeviceCounter was;	being incremented in memory but not loaded to accum before;	accum was compared with NumberOfDevices.;	Main.asm: Fixed bug: in AllDone, long for result was not pushed;	prior to call to GStrAsC1Inp, resulting in use of stack above;	allocated stack space.  Also optimized, by leaving result of;	Dereference on stack for use by GStrAsC1Inp, rather than pull/push.; 24 Jan 91	Installer.r: Added a space on either side of File and Edit menus.; 25 Jan 91	Main.asm & MainSub.asm:  ldy #^CurrentVol+2  ->  ldy #^CurrentVol;	Main.asm:  stz DialogFlag at beginning of CustomProgram to indicate ;	customized installation (previously assumed init to zero).; 28 Jan 91 V2.0d30	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 29 Jan 91	MainSub.asm: Remove ‘Export NoError’ that’s not being called.;	(It loops back to GetDInfo, which decrements SearchFlag,;	 which is not initialized coming in through NoError!); 	Main.asm: @ Real_Start: phk/plb, then stz absolute (not lda #0, sta >long ).;	Main.asm: early in StandardProgram: call to new label ConditionBtns (in VolumeSub).;	It does virtually the same, except it also calls #Active on BeginStdControl;	and it calls #Active on ‘Change Disk to Update’ control (used to unhilite btn presses);	and it conditions hi bit of var InstallRemoveMode (which may be a bug fix).;	(The rest is an optimization.); 30 Jan 91	Installer.r:  fix bug:  rToolStartup:  Font Manager wasn’t being started.;	BRC#81223: Then updated minimum version numbers to 6.0 version numbers.;	Main.asm: fix bug: KeyDown for Std Install: accum different values (anded Task.Modifiers;	and Task.Message) on two branches to Check4Arrow.  Also optimized.  Now;	Task.Message is loaded into Y, while Task.Modifiers is loaded into accum.; 30 Jan 91 V2.0d31	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 30 Jan 91	Oops.  EventMgr is not at 3.01. It’s 3.00 on ROM 01 machines. Crashes/hangs them.;	Change Installer.r back.;	Data.asm: Change Line1/Line2 text box to ‘You must start up from System 6.0 ;	or later to run the Installer.’ (prev. specified a version of GS/OS).;	Startup.asm: bug fix (above): Have error from StartUpTools put dialog, not crash/hang.;	Add label Requires6_0 to call to TLTextMountVolume.;	BRC#81308: Change GSOS version to 3.04 to signify System 6.0 minimum.;	Change unused button from Button2 (left) to Button1 (right).;	Make OKStr be button2 & use local version; make it right button by pushing it ;	left with spaces.  Do that because escape chars are counted in Button1’s ;	right justification & we added them to use MouseText returnChar after OK.;	Add label @noStartToolErr: after call to StartUpTools, if no error, bra here;;	else (error) bra to Requires6_0.;	Main.Asm: Add label MoreDone to shutdown code AFTER AllDone (after toolsShutdown,;	systemPrefs are reset, and prefixHandle is locked, dereffed, and set.;	Startup.asm: if GSOS version call isn’t high enough, jump to MoreDone,;	since tools not started, prefs not got, prefixHandle of system not got.;	Also jump to MoreDone if GStrNew fails in resizing PrefixPointer--same stuff not done.;	Move GSOS Set_Sys_Pref call to below GStrNew call so previous sentence is true.; 31 Jan 91	Oops. Startup.asm: Bank was not being restored before jml AllDone & jml MoreDone.;	This was also true in CustomDialog. (No plb’s before jml’s anywhere in Installer.);	Main.asm:  remove StandardDrawExit (not being used).;	Startup.asm / Main.asm:  Turns out that ShutDownTools does NOT do the right;	thing if error in StartUpTools returns a bogus-enough answer.;	So if error in StartUpTools, do jump to new label AlmostAllDone, which;	is AFTER call to ShutDownTools (rather than jump to AllDone).;	Note: ResourceShutdown is no longer called in the one case when;	the OS is the correct version but the tools are not.  Leaving the resource;	fork of the Installer open after the program quits (meaning you can’t;	copy a new version over the top of the old one).; 31 Jan 91 V2.0d32	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  4 Feb 91	Installer.r: start Scrap Manager to support NDAs.;	Installer.r: ;	BRC#81533: Standard Update: update FolderPriv CDEV;	BRC#81735: Standard Update: update VideoKeyboard DA;	BRC#81736: Standard Update: update StyleWriter driver;	BRC#81734: Standard Update: do not update ADU;	BRC#81739: Standard Update: do not update Shaston 16;	Installer.asm: AmendScript: bug fix: limit add of FileSpecField size to a byte;	(load from [<ZPTemp2] first, then and #$00FF, then add 1,s).;  4 Feb 91 V2.0d33	Part of system 6.0d24 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  4 Feb 91	WS#BK285: Std Update: Installer.r: change CDEV to CDevs in delete scripts.;	Installer.r: Add fDrawIconInResult and fDrawArrowIcon to ;	rControlTemplate(popUpCtl)’s ctlMoreFlags field.;	Installer.r: Add fCtlCanBeTarget and fCtlWantEvents to;	rControlTemplate(SelectListCtl) and (ScriptListCtl)’s ctlMoreFlags fields.;	Rearrange picture to make room for TargetControl emboldening of lists.;	Main.asm: Remove not-in-control beeping.;  5 Feb 91	Main.asm: apple-tab to swap list controls as the target in custom install.;	Fix bug: KeyDown for Custom Install: accum different values (anded Task.Modifiers;	and Task.Message) on two branches to Check4Arrow.  Also optimized.  Now;	Task.Message is loaded into Y, while Task.Modifiers is loaded into accum.;	Main.asm: fix bug: Custom KeyDown: Apple-Shift-O was branching to Eject,;	not Open.;  6 Feb 91	Main.asm: commented out, at StandardProgram’s AllDone, saving error codes/status;;	not used by calling routine, Real_Start.;	Main.asm: fix bug: Custom: after @NotWriteEnabled, code branches to InitControls;;	branch should have been to InitTaskMaster.;	Optimized CustomProgram.;	Main.asm: in CustomProgram’s KeyDown, add SendEventToCtl for keystrokes;	not used elsewhere (to allow moving up and down the two lists).;	Sort Application Folder list:;	MainSub.asm: add call to SortList2 after call to NewList2 in NewList2Call.;	In MakeNewList, move call to NewList2Call to before 1st member is selected (or;	not, depending on whether it’s active or dimmed).;	replace ListHandle2 with AppFolderListHdl.;	Main.asm: add emAutoKey to event mask TaskMaster is looking for in both event loops.