here (cr) or '-', leave ScriptParentLevel @ $FFFF;;	if '0' to '9' then convert to 0 to 9 and store to ScriptParentLevel;;	else report error.; 13 Feb 91	Subroutines.asm: Check4Scripts: remove unused label ItsOK.;	Data.asm: Add word var oScriptNameField.;	Installer.Equates: Remove equ ScriptNameField.;	Subroutines.asm: ReadScriptHeader: determine location of ScriptName field;	and store to oScriptNameField.;	Subroutines.asm: Check4Scripts: replace Immediate references ;	to ScriptNameField with Absolute references to oScriptNameField.; 	Subroutines.asm: Check4Scripts: fix bug: adds three using increment: ;	inx / bne around next instruction / inc a;	- except that third inc a (after @000) is an iny (perhaps high was in Y once?).;	Change iny to inc a.; 	Subroutines.asm: Check4Scripts: fix bug: jsr to GetScriptNameLength;	is followed by sta and txa.  GetScriptNameLength is only documented;	as returning accum.  Turns out last instruction in GetScriptNameLength;	is a txa, so this currently works.  Removed the txa in Check4Scripts.; 	Subroutines.asm: Check4Scripts: optimizations: in repeated cases,;	accum is used to pull both low and hi, then they are reloaded for an ;	addition.  After @1 after CheckTheEntry, change to pull hi with X, add to ;	existing lo in accum, txa to get hi for hi add.  In another case (above ;	MoveLoop2), not only was this being done, but the final store was to the ;	interim store location.  Change to clear carry, pull lo into accum, add and ;	store; pull hi into accum, add hi and store.;	Install.asm: Optimization: Removed routine Upper from CompareNames.;	Renamed UpperCase8bit, made it long (rtl and jsl’s to it), moved;	to Subroutines.asm.  Removed code in Subroutines.asm, replacing with;	jsl UpperCase8bit.;	Main.asm: FolderListSub (called by KeyDown): bug fix: Targetable list;	is seeing repeated alpha-char-folder-selection as double-click.;	Add check for mouse before calling double-click’s action.;	Data.asm: in strings: replaced dumb quotes ("") with smart quotes (“”).;	Data.asm: bug fix (kind of): CurScriptFile was allocated 16 bytes of;	storage; however, these days, only a pointer to a file is stored to it.;	Replaced with ds.L.;	Mid-version Projector checkin.; 18 Feb 91 V2.0d35	Part of system 6.0d25 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 15 Feb 91	Install.asm: optimized FindSeparator (was pushing value, then adding from stack!).;	Part 2 of process begun 12 Feb: use ScriptParentLevel to get extra;	prefix if ScriptParentLevel is other than $FFFF.;	Install.asm: ExtractSrcPrefix: at ExtractPrefix, first check ScriptParentLevel;	and determine and move script parent’s directory before moving prefix ;	in ZPTemp (both to SourcePfxPtr).;	Install.asm: store pointer to script pathname to Scriptfilename.; 17 Feb 91	(more of the same);	Install.asm: ExtractSrcPrefix: Fixed bug at CheckLength: accum was being ;	compared with #0, but accum had a pointer word, not the source prefix length ;	as documented and expected.  Now load src prefix length.;	Install.asm: ExtractSrcPrefix: Fixed bugs at @Search: Made no sense at all.;	Was switched to 8-bit (SEP) with no LONGA OFF to assembler; because of;	bug at CheckLength, described above, this code was never executed; else;	the cmp #SeparatorChar would have been executed in 8-bit but compiled in;	16-bit and would have crashed.;	As would have the jsl GStrResize.;	LDA in 8-bit lost the high byte of the string’s length.;	TAY in 8-bit accum risked passing a garbage high byte to the index register.;	Length was loaded, then used as an index into the same buffer, then;	incremented multiple times! (Looking at text past end of buffer!); 18 Feb 91	Install.asm: CompactScript: Fixed bug: var Index was declared, but with no;	storage, so it was using the next label’s storage, GetPfxParms, leaving a 0 ;	in the parameter count field when GSOS was called for a GetPrefix call!;	Prevented no-prefix-specified-so-use-Installer’s-prefix code from working.; 19 Feb 91	Install.asm: Fixed bug: Prefix being sought to get Installer’s prefix ;	was 1 instead of 9.;	Continuation of work to implement ScriptParent.;	Previous method of appending headerPrefix and fileSpecPath used GetPrefix.;	But a Parent may rise to a null prefix, which can't be set, or expanded from.;	Install.asm: Rewriting ProcessFileSpec to build full pathnames by hand;	(or using help of GString.Lib).; 20 Feb 91	(More of the same.); 21 Feb 91	(More of the same.); 21 Feb 91 V2.0d36	Released directly to testing.  Not part of a system release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 22 Feb 91	Subroutines.asm: Fixed bug in old routines that nixed new routines;	with scripts double-clicked on in Finder: Scripts were being passed;	in with slashes rather than colons and never translated to colons.;	In CheckMsgCenter: translate slashes to colons in scriptnames from;	Message Center.; 24 Feb 91	Add disk initialization for unformatted disks.;	Mainsub.asm: NextDevice: If error from Volume call is drvrIOError;	(i/o error), then offer to format the disk (by calling Format).;	If user cancels or format fails, eject disk and go on.; 25 Feb 91	Installer.r: Update Std Update script:;	Sound, Slots, and Keyboard CDevs moved to SecondDisk;;	Update-only for SetStart (decreases size of minimum Std Install);;	update Shaston 16 font;;	WS#BK327: Update more Courier fonts;;	WS#BK328: Update more Geneva fonts;;	WS#BK326: Update more Helvetica fonts (note:no updates using fourth disk);;	WS#BK329: Update more Times fonts (note:no updates using fourth disk);;	WS#BK330: Update more Venice fonts (note:update Venice 24, not the 14 in bug report);;	Delete, not Install, for System.Setup:CDEV.Init (no longer needed --Dave Lyone).;	Startup.asm: Require GSOS vs 4.0 (up from 3.4) to support new Format call.; 25 Feb 91 V2.0d37	Part of system 6.0d26 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 28 Feb 91	Installer.r: Changed Standard Update script: ;	WS#BK337: GSCalc.NDA to Calculator.NDA.;  1 Mar 91	BRC#82707: Fixed NetWork:Server Startup script.;	BRC#80388: Fixed Installer ERS screen shot.;  3 Mar 91	Install.asm: StandardUpdateSub: Fixed bug: ReleaseResource is  ;	called to get rid of the StdUpdateScript, but the handle wasn’t ;	unlocked first.  Now unlock it.;  4 Mar 91 V2.0d38	Part of system 6.0d27 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -;  4 Mar 91	Installer.r:  Replaced flag-specified Dividing Line in menus with ;	string-specified disabled-dash Dividing Line to match other;	system 6.0 application menus.;	Main.asm:  Fixed bug: In Custom Install, Apple-Tab would switch;	target lists even when the right (folder selection) list was;	inactive.  Now test DirSelReq flag before make window switch.;  5 Mar 91	Installer.r: CompactScript: Validated new PreventBootFlag ScriptFlag.;	Mainsub.asm: Fixed bug: (reading code): Dir_Reader: only a word;	was being stored to PointerSize, but PointerSize+2 was being added;	to determine end of block.  Changed PointerSize+2 to #0000.;	Changed PointerSize from ds.b 4 to ds.b 2 (given that block is;	allocated as noBankCross, the size must be <64K anyway.;	Mainsub.asm: Fixed bug: found by Dave Lyons: The Installer was;	“borrowing” bit 0 of the Member Flags byte in list Member Records;	to flag inactive folders (AppleShare, I think).  This was an;	unused bit in Toolbox Ref Vol 1 (p.11-6), but reserved.  And now;	is used, along with bit 1, by the List Manager to flag items as;	being handles or resource IDs rather than pointers for SortList2.;	“Jay” had a spare byte following every string with the flag;	already in it: he’d built an array of strings and flag bytes;	first, then built an array of Member Records, transferring the;	flag byte from one array to the other.  ;	Fix:  Dir_Reader:  ANDed out bit 0 during the transfer;;	PrintListMem:  look to flag at end of string for inactive folder flag.;	WS#MS435INS: Data.Asm: Changed dialog (re not able to determine space) ;	text from “‘foreign’ format” to “non-ProDOS disk”.;	Remove: ‘The “Disk to Update:”’ from beginning of the text; substitute;	^0 for substitution with the volume name.;  6 Mar 91	Install.asm: CalcAndCopy: Use ParamText to set substitution text;	to the volume name.;	Modified dialog’s alertTemplate to meet Human Interface Note #10.;	Mainsub.asm: SimpleKeyFilter: Fixed bug: Had RTS, not RTL at end.;	Optimized SimpleKeyFilter.;	Install.asm: CalcAndCopy: Reinstalled SimpleKeyFilter as an input ;	parameter to the non-ProDOS-disk dialog.; 10 Mar 91	Data.asm: Changed 'Latest Sys' to ' System ' as the partial name;	that a script's ScriptName should begin with in order for that;	script to be the first selected script to be read in (if boot code,;	must be first FileSpec; remaining filespecs are arranged so that;	boot disk created will boot with optimal speed).  Updated all doc;	to match.; 11 Mar 91	Mainsub.asm: Reinstalled SimpleKeyFilter as an input parameter to the;	ReBoot dialog (see 6 Mar fix).;	Mainsub.asm: Add SimpleKeyFilter as input parameter to;	the Error dialog (allow Esc to make Error dialog go away).;	Install.asm: WS#MS438INS: Caution: increase size of Caution;	dialog box to accomodate more text.  Modified dialog’s ;	alertTemplate to meet Human Interface Note #10.; 11 Mar 91 V2.0d39	Part of system 6.0d28 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -; 12 Mar 91	MainSub.asm: scanDevices: doc says it returns carry to;	indicate insertion occurred.  But carry was only being set,;	never cleared, so on disk removal of LAST (lowest-numbered);	device online, carry was returned set, so calling routine;	tries to open the ‘newly inserted’ (but really just;	ejected) disk, and GS/OS finds the