ays,  	except INSTALL SetStart if: 1) install new Start (System 	folder didn't exist); or 2) if Finder was Start, so we're	installing new Start (and Finder as Finder).		Major bug discovered:	Standard Update resource is loaded, then amended, then	compacted, then released and unlocked; but a second Standard	Update will not reload the resource, so it starts with	whatever remnants are in memory based on the target of the	previous Standard Update, and this time makes any amendments	to the end of the original length way beyond the current	end of the script.  In other words, it's bogus!	Fixed by calling DisposeHandle on ScriptHdl at end of 	each Standard Update.	And remove code added to remember size of resource, used to fix	the half of bug found on March 19 (the resource could grow; I	missed the fact that it could also shrink).17 Apr 91	Install.asm: Remove yesterday’s DisposeHandle and replace	PurgeLevel3 with DisposeNow as the Purge Level to the	ReleaseResource call on the Standard Update script.		Installer.r: 	change Slinky to A2.RAMCard;	add line to delete Finder.Icons.	; 17 Apr 91 V2.0d45	Not part of a system build release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -	Installer.r: Add line to delete A2.Slinky.19 Apr 91	BRC# 80868 / WS# BK257: Install.asm: Subtract from 	TotalBlocksForInstall, used for the total for the	thermometer, filespecs being deleted due to 	unnecessary updates.  Thermometer now updates correctly.		Install.asm: Fixed bug found reading code: CalculateSpace:	On Remove, all that’s executed is a BIT and a bra to RTS.	But caller expects carry clear unless there’s a problem.	Now bra is to lda #0000 / clc.		Install.asm: add SortSource:	A compacted script is in memory,	but any particular source disk may be scattered	through the filespecs.	Organize the filespecs so that scattered source file disks 	are together.	Get another piece of memory the same size as the script	and move filespecs there, one by one.	If not enough memory is available, stick with the original	script.20 Apr 91	SortSource.21 Apr 91	Brand new Standard Update interface, designed by Matt	Deatherage (who in DTS also supports the Mac Installer),	complete with a name change from Standard Update to Easy Update,	button name changes, 	making the "Install" button the default button,	converting the "Customize" button from an icon to a simple button,	changes to the Easy Update help screen,	and adding a modicum of help text in the window itself.	It now better matches the Macintosh Easy Update user interface,	and feels much cleaner.	Disk name is a substitution string, and updated in	an entirely different manner from before.22 Apr 91	Turn blastText bits on in many Custom Keyboard Shortcuts strings	to reduce code and display help screen faster.	Add a few pixels space in new Easy Update screen.	Change button name from “Install” to “Easy Update” and	screen and help text to match.	Removed “v2.0” from window title (it’s now in lower left corner).	23 Apr 91	Turn blastText bits on in two Customized Installation and	one Easy Update (“v2.0”) strings.	BRC# 78832 / WS# BK238: Fixed.	Adjusted center button size / location so they’re centered	between the two lists.24 Apr 91	Easy Update script:	Fixed “System.CDevs:Namer” to “System:CDevs:Namer” update;	Removed Tool037 update (Animation Tool Set, no longer	linked to 6.0).23 Apr 91	Data.asm: changed sort scriptnames leading characters for	system software scripts from “ System ” to “*System ”.	; 23 Apr 91 V2.0d46	Part of system 6.0d33 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -25 Apr 91	MainSub.asm: Fixed bug with new Easy Update dialog:	all disks offline was writing message to menu bar.		Install.r / Data.asm: Increased width of Easy Update	dialog 14 pixels so disk name is on line by itself;	invalidated *two* rects, so that internationalization	will be easi