x bug?), so relock it after.	; 21 Jun 91 V2.0d52	Part of system 6.0d41 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -23 July 91	MainSub.asm: Dir_Reader: after DeRef implemented 20 June,	push registers rather than PEAs.		MainSub.asm: NewList2Call: since SortList2 is unlocking	AppFolderListHdl (unforgiveably but, Dave claims, acceptably),	pass it a pointer to the AppFolderList instead 	(Dave’s workaround: the AppFolderList MUST remain locked,	since it’s a structure of pointers to list members	IN THE SAME MEMORY BLOCK!).		; 24 Jul 91 V2.0d53	Part of system 6.0d44 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -25 July 91	BRC# 80869, Install.asm: Amendments: 	earlier Finders not being updated because of logic error in code:	reverse bne's to beq's @ Check4Old to fix.		Rework disk-size check so that Easy Updates to 3.5" 800K floppies	don't install SetStart as START (new disk installations already	were installing Finder as START).	NOTE: Test carefully: there are lots of cases!, including: 		No System folder: create one; if 800K, install Finder as Start;	  else >800K, so install SetStart as START, Finder, SetStart CDEV.	System folder but no START: don't install Finder orSetStart as START,	  but update Finder and SetStart CDEV if they exist.	Early 6.0 Finder is START: 	  if 800K, install Finder as Start, update SetStart if it exists;	  else >800K, so install SetStart as START, Finder, SetStart CDEV.	Finder 1.0, Finder 1.1, Finder 1.2, or Finder 1.3 is START:	  use 800K test above (test each case separately!).	SetStart is START: update START with new SetStart;	  also update SetStart CDEV and Finder if they exist.	Unique (third-party) START: update SetStart CDEV and Finder	  only if they exist; don't touch START.26 July 91	Moved test for SCSI card from Install.Asm to Startup.Asm	(StartTools); store result in new var GotSCSICard.30 July 91	Added Help menu items for ‘Creating a New System Disk’, 	‘Updating an Existing Disk’, ‘Hard Disk Initialization’.	Main.asm: Installer: delete the three items if 	the RDiskNames resource is missing (developer feature:	no Easy Update, therefore no system disk creation special help).		BRC# 86766 / WS# BK400 fixed (can’t get to Easy Update	when no RDiskNames resource).		BRC# 87096 / WS# BK418: Main.asm: Installer: write a zero	to Help_GotoEasy & Help_LeftArrow, the last dialog items in 	the Customized Keyboard Shortcuts Help 	dialog, ‘Go to Easy Update’, if there’s no RDiskNames resource, 	since then there’s no Easy Update to go to.31 July 91	Attach windows to new Help menu items.2 August 91	BRC# 1009240: Eject bug: Mainsub.asm: CheckCharacter:	logical AND was being made with equate RAMorROMdisk	but immediate addressing mode wasn't used, so value came from	random memory; then beq was used instead of bne!	how this worked as often as it did...		Put up 'Hard Drive Initialization' menu command only if	SCSI Manager/SCSI.HD driver and SCSI card are installed.		Release new ERS.		Easy Update script: At Tim Swihart's behest, remove QuickConsole:	Delete { "System:System.Setup:QuickConsole" }.		Easy Update script: Remove the deletions put in during March	and April to delete file names used prior to those months but	renamed.		; 5 Aug 91 V2.0d54	Part of system 6.0d45 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -5 August 91	Startup.asm: BuildScriptList remove unneeded sec 	just before ReportError.	BRC# :Add clc just before BuildListExit to indicate no error!6 August 91	Data.asm: Hard Drive Init help message: move period before paren	(per Dave's observation).		Data.asm: Changed 'OK' to 'Quit' in 'you must use sys 6.0'	dialog.		Installer.r: Added Integer math (vs. 0300) to tools being	started up.7 August 91	Scrambler bug reading scripts going from Easy to Customize	(hangs or puts invalid pathname dialog):	Jay was using his GString library:	Startup.asm: FindScripts: GStrNew passes back a pointer; 	GStrResize passes back a pointer; 	but he passed the pointer in registers to a 	subroutine, AddScripts, that called GStrResize but never passed 	the new pointer back --	making both the next use of outputPath, and the GStrDispose invalid	(actually, there was a possibly correct GStrDispose on the pointer	where it was stored by the subroutine, but it was followed by	another GStrDispose on the original pointer, which at that	point could have been attached to ANY handle)!	So get the handle right after creating the GString from its pointer.	And reestablish the pointer after each AddScripts call	(Startup.asm: FindScripts).8 August 91	BRC# 88355: Subroutines.asm: AddScripts:	tested ScriptListSize to determine if any scripts were seen 	before setting flag ScriptListBuilt.12 August 91	Cut uncalled code: Check4Scripts.14 August 91	BRC# 80867: Install.asm: ResizeScriptMemory: was unlocking	the handle ScriptHandle, then resizing and relocking ScriptHdl!15 August 91	Installer.r: Add preload attribute flag to menu-related 	resources.		Installer.r: Add #if defined SystemSoftware around Easy Update	resources (not needed for Developer Version).		MakeFile: Updated to build both Installer and Installer.Dev	(the developer version).16 August 91	Updated Greg's Make script to build Installer.Dev.	Updated AUG:BuildEverything to build Installer.Dev.		BRC# 1010027: Fixed Matt Ackeret-found bug:	UniDisk3.5 driver was being installed every time by 	Easy Update! (Original code missing a branch.)		Easy Update script: add line to Delete { "System:ExpressLoad" }.		Main.asm: Installer: For build of developer version: 	Remove code @ NoEasy that removes three Help menu items,	since they're no longer being created as resources.		; 19 Aug 91 V2.0d55	Part of system 6.0d46 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -23 August 91	Install.asm: Updated UniDisk3.5 check to look at the	DIB's DevCharacteristics word for the GeneratedDriver bit 	before testing the SmartPort word for UniDisk3.5 value	(it's only in extended DIBS, which don't exist with	generated drivers).		BRC# 1010027: Install.asm: Jay was adding DevListHeaderSize,	not the correct DevListFieldSize, between DIB records.26 August 91	BRC# 80870: Mainsub.asm: BuildDirName:	index registers were being set to 8-bit, preventing them	from counting & indexing pathnames longer than 255 characters.27 August 91	BRC# 86277: Data.asm: interchange 9's and E's to swap	yellow and green in RAMdisk icon, and add black teeth into	the connector.		BRC# 86276: Main.asm: set up AlertMsg after (not before)	checking the selected scripts (ScriptListSub).30 August 91	BRC# 87838: Main.asm: dim/restore to active: the Easy Update	and Change Disk buttons around the call to the routine that	handles the Easy Update installation. Subroutinize EasyBtnDim	and EasyBtnActive.		BRC# 89036: MainSub.asm: Subroutinize NewFolderDim and	NewFolderActive.	MainSub.asm: SetInstallRemove: check for bWriteProtect bit	in InstallRemoveMode and check DirSelReq and set New Folder	button accordingly.	MainSub.asm: CheckScript: also check bWriteProtect bit	in InstallRemoveMode before making New Folder button active.3 September 91	BRC# 89037: Main.asm: Each time through both event loops,	check the front window to see if there's been a change between	Installer and DA windows. If change to DA window: disable Help 	menu; enable Edit menu; enable Close menu item. If change to	Installer window, do the opposite: enable Help menu; 	disable Edit menu; disable Close menu item.	Create routines TestTopWindow and DoSysChange.		; 3 Sep 91 V2.0d56	Part of system 6.0d47 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -9 September 91	Disable Erase Disk... menu item when DA is front window:	Main.asm: DoSysChange: disable, restore;	Main.asm: Installer: initialize new var EraseDiskState;	Mainsub.asm: DisableEraseDiskMenu / EnableEraseDiskMenu:	store DisableMItem / EnableMItem to EraseDiskState for	restore in DoSysChange.11 September 91	Issued ERS 2.0-8.12 September 91	Subroutines.asm: CheckMsgCenter: optimized while looking for	bug: brl->bne; comment out sty right after ldy.13 September 91	BRC# 82706: Subroutines.asm: CheckMsgCenter: 	while matching Message Center script names against those already	found, in 8-bit accumulator/memory mode, the indexes were	being incremented in memory -- but of course only 8 bits of them!	(inc ySrc; inc yDest).	Also optimized: A second comparison with "/" for conversion	to ":" was being done after the entire script from 	the Message Center had already been converted to have ":"s.	Also fix latent bug: a Message Center script name, if it didn't	match any already listed script names, would be checked	against random memory in the last check: the index was off by	one.16 September 91	Install.asm: CheckForReBoot: optimized plb/plb -> pla in	removing temporary storage from the stack.		BRC# 1006431: Install.asm: CheckForReBoot: improved the	check of CurDirPtr vs. VolStrBuffer (boot volume).		Left list (script list) is being trashed because 	scanDevices: DrawOneCtl unlocks the ScriptListHdl.	It's Subroutines.asm: Alphabetize that passes ScriptListHdl 	to NewList2; instead pass ScriptListPtr.		; 16 Sep 91 V2.0d57	Part of system 6.0d49 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -19 September 91	Brenda's low-mem ScriptList-gets-trashed-while-being-built	before-it's-alphabetized-even bug:	Subroutines.asm: AddToList: Lock ScriptListHdl after	calling ReBuildPointers; unlock earlier, before dereferencing	ScriptListHdl into OrigPtr.		BRC# 1008656: MainSub.asm: NextDevice:	add test for valid Application Folder Selection	list requirement before activating the popup control.		; 19 Sep 91 V2.0d58	Part of system 6.0d50 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -19 September 91	Brenda's low-mem ScriptList-gets-zeroed-going-to-Easy-Update,	doing-Easy-Update, and-coming-back bug:	Subroutines.asm: Alphabetize:	Test flag for Customized window before assigning newly	alphabetized list to the Control's handle (since that handle	doesn't exist when the Customized window is closed).20 September 91	Startup.asm: move from BuildScriptList to CustomDialog	(so it gets executed EVERY time the customized window is	put up, not just the first time): code to load the	ScriptList's resource template (& add code to set its	purge level to unpurgeable (0)), and stuff the address of the list	and the list item to scroll to into the control's template 	information.		Now the low-memory situation breaks the list of script files, 	a data structure just like the list of script names and the 	list of files and folders in the directory to install to:	six-byte pointers and flags followed by the names themselves.	(The major difference is that this data structure is not attached	to an on-screen scrollable list, but is sorted at the same time	as the list of scripts is so they're in sync.)	Subroutines.asm: AddToList: Lock ScriptFileHdl after	calling ReBuildPointers; unlock earlier, before dereferencing	ScriptFileHdl into OrigPtr.23 September 91	Install.asm: CopyAndDeleteFiles: optimize.	BRC# 87649: move CloseAllNDAs call from CheckForReboot 	to CopyAndDeleteFiles, so that NDAs are ALWAYS shut down 	for EVERY installation and removal to prevent 'File Open' errors.		Install.asm: CopyAndDeleteFiles: remove redundant call	to CheckForReboot.24 September 91	MainSub.asm: UpdatePopUp: modify to use InsertPathMItems,	which also results in use of system icons in popup and cuts	lots of code.	Delete most of the DeleteLoop (deletes all menu items from	previous popup); add 2 DisposeHandle calls on 	InsertPathMItems