ign icon.		BRC# 1013602:	Install.asm: CopyAndDeleteFiles:	Zero out FileHandle after disposing of it, since the check on	whether to dispose of it or not is based on whether it's zero.		BRC# 1013684:	Startup.asm: StandardDialog: Fixed random error number:	accumulator was not being saved and restored, unlike status reg.	Startup.asm: FindScripts: In the case of a mounted file server	that's no longer shared (privileges removed), searching each	volume by device number makes it thru the Volume call, at which\	point it calls:	Subroutines.asm: AddScripts: which attempts to open the 	directory. A directory open failure was passed back and aborted	the window switch to Customized.	Changed AddScripts to put up an error message but go on 	to next device.7 October 91	BRC# 1006936:	Data.asm: changed 'Creating a New System Disk' help message	to specify that new system disks must be 'ProDOS-formatted only'.	Also added '1.4-Meg' after 'FDHD' to help identify it.		; 7 Oct 91 V2.0d60	Part of system 6.0d52 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -7 October 91	Changed 'cancel' to 'stop' in dialog message, 'To stop hold	down the <apple> key and type a period (.).', consistent with	Finder messages.		Main.asm: Installer routine: remove D_DeviceNum=1 (redundant:	already set to 1 by previous code, a jsr to InitVolume).		Main.asm: move SCSI test and subsequent removal of 'Hard	Drive Init' help menu higher so it will be removed in 	appropriate cases even when scripts are double-clicked.8 October 91	BRC# 89220:	Main.asm: init new var SetupComplete to zero prior to	calling NextDevice1.	Mainsub.asm: NextDevice1: modify to advance to first *installable*	media, and not set any buttons (no dialog is up if SetupComplete=0).	Testing: Do lots of testing!	Testing: Please test removal of 'Hard Drive Init' menu if no	SCSI card -- both launching directly into Easy Update and 	when Installer is launched by double-clicking a script.9 October 91	Upgrade 5.0 systems with AppleShare (if AppleShare.FST exists,	install CDEVs:Network & EasyMount).	Upgrade 3.2 and 4.0 systems with AppleTalk (if ATInit exists,	install SCC.Manager, ATP1.ATROM, ATP2.ATRAM, and ATResponder).	Install.asm: Amendments.		; 10 Oct 91 V2.0d61	Part of system 6.0d53 release.; - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -13 October 91	BRC# 1013287:	Easy Update's delete was of "System:CDevs:CtlPanel.NDA".	Changed to delete of "System:Desk.Accs:CtlPanel.NDA".	(I presume there was never a "System:CDevs:CtlPanel.NDA"	that also needs to be deleted.)		BRC# 1014074 and 1013996:	MainSub.asm: CheckVolume: export VolTotalBlocks.	Install.asm: Amendments: evaluate VolTotalBlocks: 	Install SetStart if media is greater than 1 meg (2048 blocks).	Testing: I tested using RAM disk; please test with Mustang.		Install.asm: after each filespec is read and copied,	the code called CheckForInterrupt *before* seeing if there	is another filespec; this resulted in the 'Unknown-Mix'	message (unknown mixture of system versions) when nothing	more needed to be done (after the final filespec or, if only	one filespec, after it was installed) even though the	installation was complete.	Reversed the order, to see if filespecs remained *before*	calling CheckForInterrupt (user pressing Cmd-period).		BRC# 1008391:	Install.asm: UnknownMix: move 'Unknown-Mix' dialog up and	widen it slightly to 1) not cover the thermometer and 2) make	what is going on clearer (the view of the thermometer should	help the user see that the process is indeed not done and	the thermometer indeed not full).	In addition, UnknownMix also, after dismissing itself,	now calls UpdateMainDialog or UpdateEasyDialog 	to update the window that it covered.15 October 91	BRC# 1014315: Mainsub.asm: NextDevice1:	Had set D_DeviceNum to #0001 but not done GS/OS calls	to update; now also set InstallRemoveMode no-volumes-o